<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thirty Tyrants</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">404–403 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as the Thirty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Thirty Tyrants were the oligarchy of thirty men installed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> with Spartan backing after its defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a> in 404 BCE. Led by Critias, they executed some 1,500 people and seized property, until democratic exiles under Thrasybulus defeated them at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munychia">Munychia</a> and the democracy was restored in 403 BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants.jpg" alt="Thirty Tyrants" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Published by Guillaume Rouille(1518?-1589) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lysander-Sparta.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
